  "relevance_note": "A 'How I Treat' review reporting HA20 data almost entirely at group level (Table 1 percentages from published reviews and a cohort), with one individually described patient: 'In one severe and refractory case, we have referred a patient for allogeneic stem cell transplantation, who has been in drug-free remission for over 2 years after transplant'.",
  "method_note": "Read the whole paper manually; no script transcribed any table. Table 1 gives only aggregate frequencies for cohorts from cited reviews/studies (refs 3, 4, 21, 23-27) and Table 2 is a monitoring protocol, so neither yields individual rows. Table S1 (treatments reported in literature) is only named in the file; its content is not included. The only individual-level description is the single patient referred for allogeneic stem cell transplantation in the 'Treatment of HA20' section; recorded as 'unnamed person 1' (label rule 6, not a case report). This person's HA20 diagnosis is inferred from the section context ('Treatment of HA20', discussing the authors' HA20 patients); the paper prints no variant, sex, age or phenotype for this person, so no variants row (the paper does not tie a specific TNFAIP3 variant, as opposed to a chromosome 6 deletion, to this person) and no phenotypic_features rows were emitted, and all 20 checklist items are 'not reported'. vital_status 'alive' rests on 'has been in drug-free remission for over 2 years after transplant'. n_patients_reported and cohort_size_as_stated left null: the ~200 reported cases and the 185-case multicenter cohort are cited from other publications, not patients of this document. Inconsistencies noticed: the text attributes the 185-case multicenter cohort to reference (22) (He et al. 2026), but the Table 1 column header cites 'Multicenter cohort (27)', and reference 27 is He et al. 2020; Table 1 'Others (21, 23, 24, 25, 26)' includes reference 21, which also has its own column (Shiraki et al. 2025); reference 35 prints the year '2029'. None of these affected the extracted values.",
